    "body": "Sorry to ask you to rewrite this, but I think a use case which better highlights where this new attribute is useful is if the site is using `getPorts()` to check what devices are available and potentially connect to them automatically.\r\n\r\nWithout this attribute you have to call `port.open()` blindly, like in your example. With the `connected` attribute and event you can call `port.open()` only when `connected` is true, and otherwise show the port to the user and provide the option to connect (which might fail).\r\n\r\nThis matches the use case for the developer we worked with when designing this change.",
